  "tagline": "Rust cloud-native time-series database with SQL on DataFusion and InfluxDB-style ingestion.",
  "description": "CnosDB is an open-source distributed time-series database whose 2.x line was rewritten in Rust on Apache Arrow and DataFusion. It separates compute from storage, offers multi-tenancy and SQL with time-series extensions, and accepts InfluxDB line protocol, Prometheus remote write and OpenTSDB writes so existing collectors can be reused. The Beijing-based company behind it targets IoT, energy and observability workloads and sells an enterprise edition and cloud service. It is AGPL-3.0 and, while still actively released, has a small community outside China.",
